#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:280
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:282
msgid "What types can a parameter hold?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:283
msgid "Parameters can be integers, floats, booleans, strings, and lists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:285
msgid "Do parameter changes persist after a node is restarted?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:286
msgid ""
"No. Changes made with ``ros2 param set`` apply only to the current session. "
"To persist them, use ``ros2 param dump`` to save the values to a YAML file "
"and load that file when starting the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:290
msgid "Why do some parameters fail to load with ``ros2 param load``?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:291
msgid ""
"Parameters marked as read-only can only be set at node startup, not at "
"runtime. The ``qos_overrides`` parameters are read-only, which is why they "
"show ``failed`` messages when loading a parameter file into a running node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:294
msgid ""
"What is the difference between ``ros2 param dump`` and ``ros2 param load``?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:295
msgid ""
"``ros2 param dump`` saves a node's current parameter values to a YAML file. "
"``ros2 param load`` reads a YAML file and applies the values to a currently "
"running node."
msgstr ""
